cff-version: 1.2.0
title: merge-mining-research
message: "If you use this software or its datasets, please cite the project as below. Dataset licensing is documented in LICENSE-DATA."
type: software
authors:
  - name: deadmanoz
repository-code: "https://github.com/deadmanoz/merge-mining-research"
abstract: >-
  Research into Bitcoin merge mining and what it reveals about Bitcoin mining
  generally. When a sibling chain merge-mines Bitcoin, its AuxPoW commitments
  record the Bitcoin blocks miners built on (canonical and stale), their
  coinbases, and pools. The most developed aspect recovers Bitcoin stale blocks
  from those commitments, validates and attributes them to mining pools, and
  publishes reproducible recovery evidence; a marker census covers merge-mining
  commitments in the canonical chain.
keywords:
  - bitcoin
  - merge-mining
  - auxpow
  - stale-blocks
  - mining-pools
  - blockchain-research
